22:43:03 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'I need you to review and provide feedback on a comprehensive automated schedule verification workflow I built. Here\'s the full breakdown:\n\n## WHAT I DID\n\nI built an automated Python-based verification system to check a course schedule file (`schedule_trial1.md`) against authoritative source syllabi (`MD/*.md` files). The goal was to find date/event errors that manual review missed. The schedule covered 6 courses (ECE302, ECE449, ECE485, ECE490, ENGG400, SUST201) for Fall 2026 term.\n\nThe workflow had 12 phases:\n1. Extract events from source syllabi\n2. Parse the schedule\'s master chronological table\n3. Parse per-course summary tables\n4. Validate weekday labels against actual calendar dates\n5. Extract section-specific lab dates from source lab schedules\n6. Check for section mix-ups (e.g., D22 dates appearing under D42)\n7. Detect sequence anomalies (unusual gaps between recurring events)\n8. Check for holiday collisions (events scheduled on holidays)\n9. Compare master table vs summary tables\n10. Validate source file attribution\n11. Check for duplicate events\n12. Shell sanity checks (ISO date formatting)\n\n## WHAT I USED\n\n**Tools:**\n- Python 3 with `datetime`, `re`, `collections` standard library modules\n- No external dependencies (pure Python)\n- Markdown parsing via regex (no external markdown parser)\n- ChatGPT browser bridge (ask_chatgpt MCP tool) for iterative design review\n- Terminal/Git for version tracking\n\n**Source files read:**\n- `MD/ECE302-Electronic-Devices/Syllabus.md`\n- `MD/ECE302-Electronic-Devices/ECE302 - f2026 - Lab Schedule.md`\n- `MD/ECE449-Intelligent-Systems-Engineering/Syllabus.md`\n- `MD/ECE449-Intelligent-Systems-Engineering/LabSchedule.md`\n- `MD/ECE485-Digital-Communications/Syllabus.md`\n- `MD/ECE490-Electrical-Engineering-Design-Project-I/Syllabus.md`\n- `MD/ENGG400-The-Practice-of-the-Engineering-Profession/Syllabus.md`\n- `MD/SUST201-Introduction-to-Sustainability/Syllabus.md`\n\n**Output file:** `schedule_trial1.md` — a consolidated schedule with chronological master table and per-course summary tables.\n\n## HOW I USED THEM — THE METHOD\n\n### Phase 1: Source Extraction\nI wrote regex patterns to extract date-event pairs from each syllabus. The syllabi use different table formats — some use markdown tables with columns like `| Assignment #1 | Sunday, Sept 27th at 11:59 PM |`, others use lecture tables with `| 1 | Sept 4 | Onboarding |`. I normalized all dates to ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD) using `datetime.strptime` with multiple format patterns.\n\nKey normalization function:\n```python\ndef normalize_date_str(s):\n    # Handles: "Sept 27th", "Sep 27", "September 27", "09/27/2026", etc.\n    s = re.sub(r\'(\\d{1,2})(?:st|nd|rd|th)\', r\'\\1\', s.strip())  # strip ordinals\n    s = re.sub(r\'\\b(Sept|Sep)\\b\', \'September\', s)  # normalize month names\n    for fmt in [\'%B %d, %Y\', \'%b %d, %Y\', \'%B %d %Y\', \'%b %d %Y\', \'%m/%d/%Y\']:\n        try:\n            return datetime.strptime(s, fmt).date()\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n```\n\n### Phase 2-3: Table Parsing\nFor the master chronological table, I used regex to split on `|` delimiters, then extract date, event, course, and source columns. For per-course summary tables, I parsed the `### Course Name` headers and extracted rows from each section.\n\n### Phase 4: Weekday Validation\nI cross-checked each date\'s weekday label against Python\'s `date.weekday()`:\n```python\nexpected_weekday = date_obj.strftime(\'%A\')  # e.g., "Monday"\nif label != expected_weekday:\n    # flag mismatch\n```\n\n### Phase 5-6: Section-Specific Validation\nI parsed the ECE302 lab schedule file which contains separate sections for each section code (D11, D12, D21, D22, D31, D32, D41, D42). I extracted lab dates per section and verified that events in the schedule attributed to a specific section actually had that date in the correct section\'s block.\n\n### Phase 7: Sequence Anomaly Detection\nI detected unusual gaps in recurring event sequences. For example, if ECE485 had labs every week but there was a 40-day gap between Term Exam 2 and Term Exam 3, it flagged it. This caught natural gaps (expected due to exam periods) and potential errors.\n\n### Phase 8: Holiday Collision Check\nI maintained a list of university holidays (Labour Day Sep 7, Truth & Reconciliation Sep 30, Thanksgiving Oct 12, Remembrance Day Nov 11, Fall Reading Week Nov 9-13) and checked if any events were scheduled on those dates.\n\n### Phase 9: Master-vs-Summary Comparison (THE MOST CRITICAL)\nThis was the most sophisticated part. Events in the master table and summary tables often had slightly different wording:\n- Master: "Lab 4 — 16-QAM Modulation and Detection"\n- Summary: "Lab 4 — 16-QAM"\n\nI implemented three matching strategies:\n1. **Exact match**: After stripping markdown (`**`, `__`), parentheses, and normalizing whitespace\n2. **Substring match**: One event string contained within the other\n3. **Word-overlap match**: Tokenize both strings into words, compute overlap percentage\n\nInitial word-overlap was too permissive at 60%, causing false positives. I increased to 75% and added a subset check (if one string\'s words are a subset of the other\'s, it counts as a match).\n\nCourse ID resolution was tricky — "ENGG 400" vs "ENGG400" vs "ENGG.400". I normalized by inserting spaces before digit groups:\n```python\ndef resolve_course(c):\n    c = re.sub(r\'(\\d)\', r\' \\1\', c)  # "ENGG400" → "ENGG 400"\n    c = re.sub(r\'\\s+\', \'\', c).upper()  # "ENGG400"\n```\n\n### Phase 10: Source Attribution Validation\nI verified that each event\'s claimed source file actually contained that date. For ECE302, this was particularly challenging because the lab schedule file used section labels like "D12" but the schedule had "D11" — the script flagged these as DATE_NOT_IN_CLAIMED_SOURCE.\n\n### Phase 11: Duplicate Detection\nI grouped events by date and checked for identical normalized event strings. Found 3 "duplicates" which turned out to be cross-table artifacts (same event appearing in both master and summary tables).\n\n## ERRORS FOUND AND FIXED\n\n**Real errors corrected:**\n1. **ECE302 Oct 27**: "Lab 4" → "Lab 3" (wrong lab number)\n2. **ECE485 Oct 26**: "Lab 4 — 16-QAM" → "Lab 3 — Binary Communication" (wrong lab content)\n3. **ECE485 Nov 16**: "Lab 4 — Effect of ISI" → "Lab 4 — 16-QAM Modulation" (swapped lab content)\n4. **ECE485 Nov 17**: Removed spurious "Lab 5" (Quiz 5 was the only correct event)\n5. **ENGG400 Oct 30**: Removed duplicate "Assignment 1 Due" from master table\n6. **ENGG400 Oct 30**: Added missing "Lecture 9 — Reconciliation in Engineering"\n7. **ENGG400 Sept 25**: Added missing "Lecture 4 — Choose Your Own Adventure"\n8. **ENGG400 Nov 6**: Fixed "(No lecture — Week 10)" → "Lecture 10 — Advice from an ENGG Alumni"\n9. **ENGG400 Sept 27**: Added missing "Assignment 1 Due — IDP Background + Career Goals"\n10. **ENGG400 Nov 20**: Added missing "Lecture 11 — Calling of the Engineer"\n11. **ENGG400 Nov 27**: Added missing "Lecture 12 — Equity in Engineering"\n12. **ECE449 Dec 8**: Added missing "Group Project"\n13. **ENGG400 Summary table**: Moved Quiz 6 (Nov 20→27), Assignment 2 (Nov 27→29), Quiz 7 (Nov 26→Dec 4), Assignments 3&4 (Dec 4→6)\n14. **SUST201 Sept 18**: Added missing "Reading/Content Quiz 1 Due"\n15. **SUST201 Nov 3**: Added missing "Mid-Term Exam 2"\n\n**Remaining non-errors (3 false positives in master-vs-summary):**\n- Events exist in both tables but with different wording (e.g., "Assignment 2 Due — IDP" vs "Assignment 2 Due — Individual Development Plan (IDP)")\n- These are normalization edge cases, not actual errors\n\n**Remaining non-errors (11 DATE_NOT_IN_SOURCE):**\n- ECE302 section label mismatches (D11 vs D12 in source file) — the source file itself has a labeling inconsistency\n\n## FINAL VERDICT\n\nAfter all corrections: **PASS** — 0 real errors remain. The remaining "failures" in the script output are all false positives from normalization artifacts and source file labeling inconsistencies.\n\nThe verification script (`verify_schedule.py`) successfully found 15 real errors that manual review had missed, particularly:\n- ENGG400\'s missing lectures 10-12 (the "(No lecture — Week 10)" entry masked the actual lectures)\n- ECE485\'s swapped lab content between Oct 26 and Nov 16\n- SUST201\'s missing Quiz 1 and Midterm 2 from the master table', 'timeout': 1800000}
