22:46:38 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'I want to implement the improvements you recommended for my schedule verification system. Before I start coding, here\'s my plan — please review and give feedback:\n\n## PLAN: Strengthen verify_schedule.py\n\n### 1. Structured Event Model\nCreate an `Event` dataclass with fields:\n- `course` (resolved ID like "ECE485")\n- `section` (D11, D22, etc. or None)\n- `event_type` (LAB, QUIZ, ASSIGNMENT, MIDTERM, EXAM, LECTURE, etc.)\n- `event_number` (int or None)\n- `title` (descriptive text)\n- `date` (date object)\n- `time` (str or None)\n- `source_file` (path to source)\n- `source_lines` (tuple of line numbers)\n- `table_scope` (MASTER, SUMMARY_ECE302, etc.)\n- `confidence` (EXPLICIT, INFERRED, INFERRED_YEAR)\n\n### 2. Event Parser (Before Fuzzy Matching)\nBuild a parser that extracts `event_type` and `event_number` from event strings like:\n- "Lab 3 — Binary Communication" → type=LAB, number=3\n- "Quiz 5" → type=QUIZ, number=5\n- "Assignment 2 Due — IDP" → type=ASSIGNMENT, number=2\n- "Midterm 1" → type=MIDTERM, number=1\n- "Lecture 9" → type=LECTURE, number=9\n\nUse regex: `^(Lab|Quiz|Assignment|Midterm|Term Exam|Lecture|Group Project)\\s*(\\d+)`\n\n**Rule:** If both records have event_number and they differ → FAIL (no fuzzy matching allowed).\n\n### 3. Source Provenance Tracking\n- When extracting from source files, record exact line numbers\n- Create stable IDs: `course:filename:line_start-line_end`\n- Store `source_raw` (the original markdown row)\n\n### 4. Coverage Invariant\nReport at the end:\n```\nSOURCE EXTRACTION COVERAGE\nCandidates: 317\nClassified as events: 240\nRejected: 61 (with reasons: COURSE_START_DATE, OFFICE_HOURS, etc.)\nUnresolved: 16\n```\n\n### 5. Sequence Anomaly Detection by Event Family\nGroup events by (course, event_type) and analyze:\n- Ordinal ordering (Lab 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5)\n- Date ordering\n- Missing ordinals\n- Duplicate ordinals\n- Out-of-order sequences\n\n### 6. Master-Summary Compound Row Splitting\nBefore comparison, split rows containing `;` or `+` into atomic events.\nCompare `(course, date, atomic_event)` not whole rows.\n\n### 7. Duplicate Checking Within Scope\nOnly flag duplicates within the same table scope:\n- Same event twice in MASTER → potential duplicate\n- Same event in MASTER and SUMMARY → expected redundancy\n\n### 8. Date Normalization Fix\n```python\ndef normalize_date_str(s, default_year=2026):\n    # Handle dates without year: "September 27" → 2026-09-27\n    # Record year_inferred=True when default_year is used\n```\n\n### 9. Course Normalization Simplification\n```python\nre.sub(r\'[^A-Za-z0-9]\', \'\', c).upper()  # "ENGG 400" → "ENGG400"\n```\n\n### 10. Verdict Vocabulary\nReplace binary PASS/FAIL with:\n```\nSCHEDULE ERRORS: 0\nMASTER/SUMMARY STRUCTURAL ERRORS: 0\nPARSER FALSE POSITIVES: 3\nKNOWN SOURCE INCONSISTENCIES: 11\nUNEXPLAINED DISCREPANCIES: 0\nOVERALL: PASS WITH KNOWN SOURCE WARNINGS\n```\n\n### 11. Exit Codes\n- `exit 0` = verified (no real discrepancies)\n- `exit 1` = real discrepancies found\n- `exit 2` = unresolved parsing/source ambiguity\n\n### 12. Regression Test Fixtures\nCreate a function that:\n1. Copies schedule_trial1.md to a temp file\n2. Introduces known errors (Lab 3→4, date shifts, section swaps)\n3. Runs the verifier\n4. Asserts each mutation is detected\n5. Cleans up\n\n## QUESTIONS FOR YOU:\n\n1. Should I implement all 12 items, or prioritize? (I\'d suggest: 1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 11 as P0; 3, 4, 9, 12 as P1)\n\n2. For the event parser, should I handle compound events like "Lecture 3 + Quiz 2" as two separate events during parsing, or only during master-summary comparison?\n\n3. For source provenance — should I modify the source extraction to record line numbers, or is a best-effort approach (line number of first matching date) sufficient?\n\n4. Should the regression test be a separate file (e.g., `test_verify_schedule.py`) or integrated into `verify_schedule.py` as a `--test` flag?', 'timeout': 1800000}
