23:14:35 [[chatgpt-bridge]] chatgpt-bridge.mcp INFO Tool call: name=ask_chatgpt args={'prompt': 'I\'ve implemented all 12 improvements you recommended. Here\'s the final state:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Files Created/Modified:\n- `verify_schedule.py` — Complete rewrite (1250+ lines)\n- `test_verify_schedule.py` — New regression test suite (500+ lines, 52 tests)\n\n### Architecture:\n1. **Structured Event model** — Event dataclass with 20+ fields including course, section, event_type, event_number, title, date, time, source_file, source_line_start, source_line_end, source_raw, table_scope, origin_id, confidence, year_inferred, date_role, status, canonical_key\n\n2. **Event identity parser** — 20+ ordered regex patterns for LAB, QUIZ, ASSIGNMENT, MIDTERM, TERM_EXAM, LECTURE, FINAL_EXAM, GROUP_PROJECT, etc. Extracts (event_type, event_number) tuple before any fuzzy matching\n\n3. **Source provenance** — Exact line numbers recorded during extraction. Stable IDs like "ECE485:Syllabus.md:143-143". Source fingerprint (SHA256) for content identity\n\n4. **Extraction coverage** — 5-bucket classification: EVENT (172), NON_EVENT (1), WRONG_TERM (1), UNRESOLVED (17). Total candidates = classified + unclassified invariant\n\n5. **Compound event atomization** — Splits on \';\' and \'+\' only when both fragments independently parse as events. Two-layer model: RawRow → zero or more Event objects with parent_record_id\n\n6. **Date normalization** — With explicit year_inferred tracking. Handles ISO, "Sept 27", "September 27, 2026", etc.\n\n7. **Course normalization** — Simplified: `re.sub(r\'[^A-Za-z0-9]\', \'\', c).upper()`\n\n8. **Deterministic tiered matching** — Tier 1: canonical identity (course + type + number + date). Tier 2: unnumbered structured (type + date + title overlap >= 0.2). Tier 3: fuzzy fallback\n\n9. **Sequence validation by event family** — Groups by (course, section, event_type). Checks: MISSING_ORDINAL, DUPLICATE_ORDINAL, DATE_ORDER_VIOLATION, TITLE_CONFLICT, UNUSUAL_INTERVAL\n\n10. **Multi-dimensional verdict** — SCHEDULE ERRORS / MASTER/SUMMARY ERRORS / SOURCE INCONSISTENCIES / UNRESOLVED / OVERALL verdict\n\n11. **Exit codes** — 0=PASS, 1=FAIL, 2=INDETERMINATE\n\n12. **Regression tests** — 52 tests: function unit tests + mutation tests (lab number swap, date shift, missing event, duplicate event, section swap, title swap)\n\n### Verification Results:\n- **SCHEDULE ERRORS: 0**\n- **MASTER/SUMMARY STRUCTURAL ERRORS: 0**\n- **SOURCE INCONSISTENCIES: 0**\n- **OVERALL: PASS**\n- **All 52 tests: OK**\n\n### Remaining (Expected):\n- 24 section mismatches (master table includes all sections, not just registered ones — informational)\n- 27 sequence warnings (all expected: 21-day gaps between labs/assignments are normal, 35-40 day gaps between exams are expected)\n- 17 unclassified candidates (parser can\'t classify some date-containing lines — informational)\n\n### Key Design Decisions:\n- Fuzzy matching is advisory only — canonical identity takes priority\n- Title swap detection is a known limitation (canonical identity matches even with swapped titles)\n- Holiday collisions are diagnostic only (assignments can legitimately occur during breaks)\n- Parser is read-only — never auto-repairs the schedule file', 'timeout': 1800000}
