## AUDIT REPORT\n\n**ECE302:**\n- Kept D22-specific: 6 (Lab intro D21/D22, D22 Lab 1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\n- Kept course-wide: 9 (First Day, Labour Day, Truth/Reconciliation, Thanksgiving, Fall Reading Week, Remembrance Day, Midterm 1, Midterm 2, Last Day)\n- Kept E32: 0 (no E32 events in chronological list — I should check if any are missing)\n- Removed other sections: 15\n\n**ECE449:**\n- Kept: 8 (5 labs + Mid-term Exam + Group Project + course-wide labs)\n- Removed: 0\n\n**ECE485:**\n- Kept: 9 (3 labs + 6 quizzes/term exams)\n- Removed: 0\n\n**ECE490:**\n- Kept: 9 (all course-wide)\n- Removed: 0\n\n**ENGG400:**\n- Kept: 17 (all)\n\n**SUST201:**\n- Kept: 11 (all)\n\n**TOTAL:**\n- Original: 110 rows\n- Removed: 15 rows\n- Filtered: 95 rows\n\n## POTENTIAL ISSUES TO FLAG\n\n1. **E32 seminar**: The calendar shows ECE 302 SEM E32 (Wed 12:00-12:50 PM, ED 129), but there are no E32-specific events in the chronological list. Should I note this as a discrepancy?\n\n2. **ECE302 Lab intro sessions**: I kept "Lab intro session — D21 / D22 @ 2:00 PM / 3:00 PM" because it includes D22. But I removed the D31/D32 and D41/D42 sessions. This seems correct.\n\n3. **ECE449 course-wide events**: Some events like "Lab 2 — Prompt Engineering with OpenAI" don\'t have a section label. I kept them as course-wide. But are they section-specific?\n\n4. **ECE485 course-wide events**: Similarly, lab and quiz entries without section labels were kept as course-wide.\n\nPlease review this analysis. Are there any issues with my filtering logic? Should I have kept or removed anything differently? Should I have flagged any ambiguities?', 'timeout': 300000}
