ts** (no time specified):\n- First Day of Classes\n- Labour Day\n- Truth and Reconciliation Day\n- Thanksgiving Day\n- Fall Reading Week\n- Remembrance Day\n- Midterm 1 (15%) — percentage, no time\n- Midterm 2 (15%) — percentage, no time\n- Mid-term Exam (20%) — percentage, no time\n- Mid-Term Exam 1 (21.5%) — percentage, no time\n- Mid-Term Exam 2 (22.5%) — percentage, no time\n- Final Exam (45%) — this has times: Dec 7 12:00 PM – Dec 8 1:30 PM\n- Last Day of Classes\n- Discussion posts deadline — has time "11:59 PM"\n- Final discussion posts — has time "11:59 PM"\n\n**Timed events** (have explicit times):\n- Quiz Due events at 9:00 AM\n- Term Exams at 11:00 AM\n- Assignment Due at 11:59 PM\n- Assignment Due at Noon\n- Assignment Due at 4:00 PM\n- Lectures (ENGG 400) — these are recurring in calendar but in schedule they\'re one-time events. What time should I use for ENGG 400 lectures? The calendar says Fri 12:00-12:50 PM.\n- Lab intro session at 3:00 PM\n\nPlease provide a clear classification of all 84 events into:\n1. Timed events (with exact time)\n2. All-day events (date only)\n3. Range events (date range)\n\nThen confirm the creation plan:\n1. Write the file with all 10 recurring events + 84 one-time events\n2. Use deterministic UIDs\n3. Include DESCRIPTION with source provenance\n4. Use CRLF line endings\n5. Proper ICS escaping\n\nDo NOT write the file yet. Just confirm the plan and classifications are correct.', 'timeout': 300000}
